{"type":"step-attempt","step":"code-review","sessionId":"f7f633e1-2502-4bcc-814d-27be8d0e3b4e","outcome":{"verdict":"approved","findingsPath":"specrunner/changes/finding-remediation-contract/review-feedback-001.md","error":null,"toolResult":{"ok":true,"findings":[{"severity":"low","resolution":"fixable","file":"src/core/port/__tests__/remediation-parse.test.ts","title":"TC-T10-01 reproduction fixture tests buildFindingsBlock, not CodeFixerStep.buildMessage","rationale":"tasks.md §T-10 specifies the assertion should verify 'code-fixer の buildMessage 出力に両 site が同時に現れること'. The fixture at line 495 calls buildFindingsBlock([f], 'code-review') directly. While functionally equivalent (buildFindingsBlock is the sole source of sites content in buildMessage), regressions in the findingSelection step (selectFixerTargetFindings), renderEvidenceReference composition, or wrapping template would not be caught. The fixer-findings.test.ts tests do cover buildMessage end-to-end but only with generic fixtures, not the two-site cross-boundary scenario required by T-10.","line":495},{"severity":"low","resolution":"fixable","file":"src/prompts/judge-rules.ts","title":"FINDING_REMEDIATION_DEFINITION scanning obligation omits 'same-check across abstraction layers' category from design D8","rationale":"Design D8 specifies the scanning obligation as '同じ不変条件を共有する隣接関数・並列経路・同じ検査を行う別レイヤを走査し'. The fragment stops at '隣接関数・並列経路' and omits 'same-check different layer'. TC-T04-04 only checks the two-category phrase so tests pass, but reviewers are not explicitly instructed to scan across abstraction layers — precisely the pattern in the motivating evidence (commit-push.ts vs parallel-review-round.ts are different layers of the same pipeline invariant).","line":129}],"evidence":{"checked":38,"skipped":0,"unverified":0},"observations":[{"severity":"low","file":"src/core/port/report-result.ts","title":"parseRemediation validates non-empty (trimmed) but stores original untrimmed value","rationale":"parse